# Pull request write-up

This **overrides** the generic `## Summary` / `## Test plan` PR body. Every Outris GitHub PR (crypto, TraceFlow, StatementFlow, number-lookup, identity-mcp, and siblings) uses the crypto format.

When opening or editing a PR (`gh pr create`, `gh pr edit`, GitHub UI), fill this shape. If `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` exists in the repo, use it verbatim.

## Title (`gh pr create --title`)

`type(scope): imperative summary`

Types: `feat` | `fix` | `docs` | `refactor` | `ci` | `ops` | `test` | `chore`

Example: `fix(workbench): expand transfers lean so txs return before proxy drop`

## Required body sections

Write in plain engineering English. Overview is 1–3 sentences. Say what was done, why, and how to verify — not a changelog dump.

1. **Overview** — what this PR delivers
2. **Problem** — what was broken, missing, or inconsistent; user/system impact first
3. **Solution** — the approach taken, not a file list
4. **Key Changes** — concrete bullets (behavior, contracts, names); group by subsystem when large
5. **Validation / Testing** — checked = already run; unchecked = still required after review or deploy. Quote the exact command and result
6. **Risks / Compatibility** — what this can break, what stays compatible, intentional trade-offs
7. **Reviewer Notes** — where to look first; call out boundaries a diff will hide

Optional — keep only when they add information; delete otherwise:

- **Technical Details / Data Flow**
- **Deployment / Migration Notes** (schema, env, flags, post-deploy checks, or `None.`)

## Hard bans

Do **not** use:

- `## Summary`
- `## Test plan` as a top-level heading (put checks under **Validation / Testing**)
- Authorship, generator, or tooling footers of any kind, including:
  - `Made with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)`
  - `Co-Authored-By: Cursor` / Claude / Copilot / Anthropic
  - robot emoji or “Generated with …” lines
  - links to `cursor.com`, `claude.com`, `anthropic.com`, or AI tooling repos

End the body on the last content section. No footer.

## Example (abridged)

```markdown
## Overview

Wallet `chain` on Fusion canvas now survives a second Instagram promote / intake persist. Previously a later upsert wiped `TRX` and the node looked chainless after refresh.

## Problem

`case_entities` upsert replaced `attribution` on conflict. The first write often lacked chain; a later promote could not stamp `chain: TRX` onto the existing row.

## Solution

Merge `attribution` JSON on conflict and prefer artifact rows that already have a non-null chain when promoting.

## Key Changes

- `case_entities` upsert merges `attribution` instead of replacing it
- Instagram promote uses `DISTINCT ON` to keep the chained wallet row

## Validation / Testing

- [x] `pytest tests/test_case_graph_repository.py` — includes `test_wallet_attribution_chain_merges_on_conflict`
- [ ] Promote an IG profile with a TRX wallet twice — `GET /canvas/{id}/graph` keeps `chain: TRX` after refresh

## Deployment / Migration Notes

None. No schema or env changes.

## Risks / Compatibility

Existing rows without chain are unchanged until the next promote/intake write.

## Reviewer Notes

Start at the upsert merge in the case-graph repository. Product behavior is not in the Instagram OCR path.
```
